title: Psalms 33–35: Sing unto Him a New Song, and Plead My Cause
description: Psalms 33 and 35 in the King James Bible: praise with the harp and a new song, music in the church and in heaven, the word of the LORD is right, blessed is the nation whose God is the LORD, and plead my cause, O LORD, angels, loving our enemies and the prayer that does not bargain, from the Psalms series studies.
output: lessons/bible/psalms-33-35.html
context: yes

